new file mode 100644
index 0000000..40d0c42
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0002-newsletter-sign-up-as-a-self-contained-module.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [NewsletterSubscription]
+related:
+  - modules/newsletter/**
+  - guren.arch.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable-5-1/1.0", at: 2026-09-29T16:19:33.246Z }
+---
+
+# Newsletter sign-up as a self-contained module
+
+## Context
+
+Marketing wants a newsletter sign-up on the blog, and the same sign-up ships
+with the next product. It therefore has to be liftable into another app as
+is, and the blog must not grow a dependency on it.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Everything newsletter-specific lives under `modules/newsletter/`: routes,
+  controller, validators, model and the `newsletter_subscriptions` table
+  definition. `src/app.ts` registers it through `createApp({ modules })`.
+- The root `db/schema.ts` re-exports `modules/newsletter/db/schema.ts` so
+  drizzle-kit generates the table's migration into `db/migrations/`, which
+  `bun run db:migrate` applies.
+- `guren.arch.ts` forbids every file under `app/` and `routes/` from
+  importing anything under `modules/newsletter/`, type-only imports
+  included. The built-in module boundary alone would still allow the
+  module's `index.ts` and `db/schema.ts`.
+- A subscription is created pending, with a 64-character random token
+  issued by the server; `token` and `confirmedAt` are not mass-assignable.
+- Subscribe and unsubscribe redirect to the `Referer` page only when it is
+  on the request's own origin, and to `/` otherwise.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `bunx guren check` fails as soon as blog code imports the module, so the
+  separation does not depend on review.
+- Blog pages cannot call the module's code; a sign-up form posts to
+  `/newsletter/subscribe` over HTTP.
+- Moving the module to another app means copying the folder, registering it
+  in that app's `src/app.ts`, re-exporting its schema and generating a
+  migration there.
+- Sending the confirmation email is not implemented; the token is only
+  stored.
